        "original_id": "7c4b9b9e-da04-5bbd-8ee6-440ec8da498f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Conan O'Brien, Robert Smigel, Brandon Tartikoff\n- Organizations: NBC\n- Works: Lookwell\n- Roles: television executive, NBC chairman, president of NBC, writer, producer, creative voice\n\nFacts:\n- Brandon Tartikoff was born on January 13, 1949, and died on August 27, 1997.\n- Brandon Tartikoff was an American television executive and served as president of NBC from 1980 to 1991.\n- Lookwell was a television pilot written and produced by Conan O'Brien and Robert Smigel.\n- Robert Smigel later became a primary creative voice for Conan O'Brien's late night show.\n- Brandon Tartikoff, as NBC chairman, considered Lookwell a personal favorite.\n- NBC did not pick up Lookwell as a series.",
